  {
    "sha": "41f8b10049c280fdbf1f22dd3331e11c7fb73fe4",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDQxZjhiMTAwNDljMjgwZmRiZjFmMjJkZDMzMzFlMTFjN2ZiNzNmZTQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T02:11:16Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T02:11:16Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(geometry): read OBJECTS of an AC1015 DXF as inert records\n\nAC1015 exports put a group 102 reactor bracket in each object and write\nLAYOUT, ACDBDICTIONARYWDFLT and ACDBPLACEHOLDER objects next to the\ndictionaries. The reader refused the first bracket (\"DICTIONARY:\nunsupported dictionary group 102 or value\") and every object type other\nthan DICTIONARY, so the real files did not import.\n\nA balanced, non-nested 102 bracket is now opaque. A DICTIONARY keeps all\nits field checks. Other objects are inert: the reader takes only the\nhandle and the owner from the common header and adds the object to the\nownership graph of #3176. Unowned objects, stray entities (AcDbEntity),\nbroken brackets and a missing ENDSEC stay named errors. The reader\nkeeps no OBJECTS data, so no object can change the imported geometry.\n\nThe real q04 export now gives the same 2 closed chains as its R12 twin.\n\nFixes #3450\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
